 # Hybrid Volume Rendering
-Also called: Mixed Geometry Rendering, Hybrid Ray Tracing
+Also called: Mixed Geometry Rendering
 
 ## Overview
-Hybrid Volume Rendering is a method for mixing geometric and volumetric data by casting rays through the ensemble of both, drawing samples of each, and compositing them in depth-sorted order [S4, unofficial]. It solves the problem of rendering scenes containing both polygonal models (e.g., surgical instruments, surface meshes) and volumetric data (e.g., CT/MR scans) in a single pass with correct visibility and attenuation [S2, unofficial]. Unlike pure volume rendering which rasterizes slices, or pure ray tracing which handles only geometry, this method simultaneously traces rays through volumetric sample arrays and polygonal databases, resampling both at equally spaced intervals to handle mixtures of geometric and volumetric data [S4, unofficial]. It is distinguished from slice-based or proxy-geometry rasterization by its explicit ray-casting approach to mixing [S4, unofficial].
+Hybrid Volume Rendering is a method for mixing geometric and volumetric data by casting rays through the ensemble of both, drawing samples of each, and compositing them in depth-sorted order [S3, unofficial]. It solves the problem of rendering scenes containing both polygonal models (e.g., surgical instruments, surface meshes) and volumetric data (e.g., CT/MR scans) in a single pass with correct visibility and attenuation [S2, unofficial]. Unlike pure volume rendering which rasterizes slices, or pure ray tracing which handles only geometry, this method simultaneously traces rays through volumetric sample arrays and polygonal databases, resampling both at equally spaced intervals to handle mixtures of geometric and volumetric data [S4, unofficial]. It is distinguished from slice-based or proxy-geometry rasterization by its explicit ray-casting approach to mixing [S4, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
-The method consists of two primary variants: the **Hybrid Ray Tracer** (direct ray casting through mixed data) and **3D Scan-Conversion** (converting geometry to volume) [S4, unofficial]. The Hybrid Ray Tracer is the core method described below.
+The method consists of two primary variants: the **Hybrid Ray Tracer** (direct ray casting through mixed data) and **3D Scan-Conversion** (converting geometry to volume) [S4, unofficial]. The Hybrid Ray Tracer is the core method described below [S4, unofficial].
 
